{
  "name": "ladybird",
  "_about": "A seven-spot ladybird (Coccinella septempunctata), 7 mm long and 5.5 mm wide: a glossy near-hemispherical dome, flat underneath -- red wing cases with seven black spots (one shared at the scutellum, three on each: a small one behind the shoulder, a big one mid-length out toward the edge, one in the rear third), a broad black pronotum with a white patch at each front corner, the small black head tucked under it with two pale spots by the compound eyes, short clubbed antennae and short black legs mostly hidden under the dome, walking on a tripod gait. Coats: the two-spot ladybird (Adalia bipunctata: one spot an elytron) and its black form (two red spots on black). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py.",
